WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.034 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:03.737
is an Academy, Emmy, Grammy,
and Tony Award-winning musician.

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:06.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
His new album "Bigger Love
is on sale now,

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.675
and he's currently serving
as a coach on this season

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:11.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
of "The Voice," which airs
Mondays and Tuesdays

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:12.278 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
right here on NBC.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome back to the sho
John Legend.

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:17.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you, John?
-Hey, Seth. Good to see you.

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:18.918 line:92%
-Good to see you as well.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, a lot of people wer
celebrating this weekend.

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:25.792
You guys made it a family affair
in Los Angeles.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:26.926 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, we did.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:30.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were feeling the energy
around us

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
and seeing on social media
so many people out

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
honking their horns
and celebrating,

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:37.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we were like,
"Let's get out of the house.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's go and interact
with the people."

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we went out
to West Hollywood,

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:43.877 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Santa Monica Boulevard,

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:47.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there was an impromptu
dance party happening,

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:49.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we just drove through
for a little bit

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.785 line:92%
and celebrated with the crowd.

00:00:51.785 --> 00:00:53.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We actually have
a short video here.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.755 line:92%
Here you are with the family

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:57.390 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hey!

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:02.829 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Crowd cheering ]

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:05.098 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Whoo!

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:08.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It should be noted, to a lo
of voters in America,

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's what West Hollywood
always looks like.

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:12.005 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:13.940 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Yes. That's a fair --

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.609 line:92%
that's a fair approximation.

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:17.677 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughs ]

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:21.514
But it was really nice to
celebrate with everybody.

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:24.918
-That's great. I want to ask
as well, about "The Voice.

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:27.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
Very exciting to have anothe
season going.

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:30.790 line:92%
How's it been for you so far

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's been so good.
You know, this is our

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:36.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
first season
in the COVID environment

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:40.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we were able to go bac
to the studio

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:44.270
and with all of these new
protocols, tape the show,

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the talent hasn't
changed a bit.

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:52.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
In fact, I've said that
this year's blind audition

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:54.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
were the best group of singers
that we've had

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.784
since I've been on the show,
which this is my fourth season

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:00.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I'm really impressed
with the artists

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:03.723
that we're able to work with
and I think we're putting on

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
a really great show
for the country.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is so exciting
to watch any kind of

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
live performance these days,
and the show's done

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:11.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
such a good job
of grabbing that.

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:14.400
Of course, there are reall
strong COVID protocols in place.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
We talked to Gwen about
how she used a T-shirt canno

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:20.406 line:92%
to shoot T-shirts to her team.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.641 line:92%
You took a different approach.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can't quite tell what
we're talking about

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:26.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
with this picture there,
but this close-up

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:29.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
really brings home
how creepy that is.

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:30.917 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Was that your idea?

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:36.523 size:84% position:42%
-I took a substantially
inferior approach to --

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:37.590 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:42.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Voice" producer suggested
I use a rubber hand

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:44.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
to reach out and shake
everyone's hand,

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:47.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you can see how creepy
it looks.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:52.505
And, I make fun of myself and my
glove for the entire season,

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:55.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
and deservedly so.
[ Laughs ]

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You -- I know
you have new music.

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:59.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have a new album.
-Yes.

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:01.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Obviously, you're not alone
in being a performer

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
who hasn't been able to get ou
and do live shows.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you hopeful you'll be able
to do that soon?

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
And how badly
have you missed it?

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:10.790
-Well, with the good news
about the vaccine today,

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:14.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm hopeful that the world
can get back to normal

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.029 line:92%
by the middle of next year

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:18.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a tour scheduled
for August.

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:22.068
We postponed it from this year's
August to next year's August

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:24.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we'll see
if it's able to happen,

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:27.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I think the news
about the vaccine

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
makes that a little more
possible.

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:32.445
-You're doing a song for u
tonight later in the show

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:33.146 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
called "Wild."

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:35.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was the inspiration
behind that song?

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:41.454
-Well, it's a song about being
in love, and being passionate.

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.356 line:92%
And the video, of course,

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:46.526 line:92%
featured my wife and our family,

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:48.595 line:92%
and it's a really powerful song.

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:53.299
Also features the great
Gary Clark Jr. on guitar.

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's not on our performanc
tonight,

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.337 line:92%
but he's on the album version.

00:03:57.337 --> 00:04:01.474
And I -- it's really one of my
favorite songs on the album,

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:02.942 line:92%
one of Chrissy's favorites

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:05.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
and hopefully everyone
loves it tonight.

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:07.513
-I want to end that you were
in Philly with your family

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:10.683
again supporting -- this was
the night before the election,

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:13.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
so before he was
president-elect.

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:15.121 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.389 line:92%
-Was that a special night?

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:17.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you enjoy being there
supporting?

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:20.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was so special.
We wanted to be there to help.

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:23.796
We knew that Pennsylvania
was going to be close,

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:26.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we knew that if
we could drive up turnout

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
in Philadelphia
and the surrounding areas,

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:31.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Joe Biden would have
a chance to win.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:34.340
And Philly came through,
Pennsylvania came through,

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
other states around the countr
came through.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:40.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we're very, very excited
that Joe Biden

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:42.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the president-elect
of the country.

00:04:42.649 --> 00:04:47.287 align:start size:94% position:6%
We need someone with his
leadership skills, his empathy

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:50.123 line:92%
his intelligence, his team

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:53.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
We think it's going to be much
better for the country.

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:55.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I'm neither here
nor there on it,

00:04:55.328 --> 00:04:57.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I'm not political.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.597 --> 00:04:58.564 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Clearly.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:01.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
Absolutely neutral!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, thank you so much
for being here.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:06.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
And thank you, as well,
for doing the song for us.

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:07.540 size:88% position:44% line:92%
We can't wait to see it.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:09.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always a pleasure
to see you.

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:10.009 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Love to your family.

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:12.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you, Seth.
Great to see you too.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:13.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Bigger Love" is out now,
and "The Voice" airs

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:16.482 size:75% position:38%
Mondays and Tuesdays
right here on NBC.

